# Act One

= Maya keeps the light burning on the night the supply boat is late.

FADE IN:

EXT. NORTH POINT LIGHTHOUSE - NIGHT

Rain sheets across black rocks. At the top of a white tower, a lamp turns slowly, throwing a long beam over the water.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - CONTINUOUS

MAYA OKAFOR (40s, oilskin coat, steady hands) trims a wick with a pair of brass scissors. A radio crackles on the bench behind her.

TOMAS (V.O.)
(through static)
North Point, this is the Gull. Do you read?

Maya grabs the handset.

MAYA
I read you, Tomas. You're three hours late.

TOMAS (V.O.)
Engine trouble. We're drifting east of the shoals.

CLOSE ON THE CHART TABLE

A pencil line marks the shoals. Maya's finger traces the drift. It runs straight into the rocks.

MAYA
Listen to me. Keep the beam on your port side. Whatever happens, keep it on your port side.

TOMAS (V.O.)
And if the light goes out?

MAYA
It won't.

[[Check: is the lamp oil or electric in 1952? Keep it oil.]]

The lamp GUTTERS. The flame shrinks to a blue bead.

MAYA (CONT'D)
(under her breath)
Don't you dare.

CUT TO:

EXT. THE GULL - DECK - NIGHT

A small fishing boat pitches in the swell. TOMAS BELL (60s, soaked, cheerful even now) wrestles the wheel. His grandson ARI (12) clutches a rail.

ARI
I can't see it anymore.

TOMAS
Then look harder. She's never once let it go dark.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - STAIRWELL - CONTINUOUS

Maya takes the iron stairs two at a time, a can of oil swinging from one hand.

INT. LIGHTHOUSE - LAMP ROOM - CONTINUOUS

She pours. The flame catches, climbs, BLOOMS. The beam swings out across the water again.

EXT. THE GULL - DECK - NIGHT

The beam sweeps over the boat. Ari lets out a whoop.

ARI ^
There!

TOMAS ^
Told you.

Tomas spins the wheel. The bow turns away from the rocks.

/*
An earlier draft had Maya row out to meet the boat.
Too heroic. The light is the hero.
*/

EXT. NORTH POINT LIGHTHOUSE - DAWN

Grey light. The supply boat bumps against the jetty. Maya walks down to meet it, wiping oil from her hands.

TOMAS
You look tired.

MAYA
I was up all night.

TOMAS
(grinning)
Reading?

She laughs, takes the first crate from his arms, and heads back up the path.

FADE OUT.

> THE END <
